.TH CYAML_SERIALIZE_FREE_MP 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cyaml_serialize_free_mp, cyaml_serialize_free \- free a serializer buffer
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cyaml.h>

void cyaml_serialize_free_mp(char *s, ccol_memmgmt_procs_t *mp);
void cyaml_serialize_free(char *s);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Free a buffer returned by cyaml_serialize(), cyaml_serialize_flow() or
cyaml_serialize_stream().  cyaml_serialize_free() is an inline wrapper
that passes NULL for mp.

The mp argument must match the allocator that was active when the
library created the DOM tree, that is, the mp that the caller gave to
cyaml_parse_mp() or to a create function.  Passing the wrong allocator
here is undefined behaviour.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
s    String to free.  It can be NULL, in which case the function does
     nothing.
mp   Allocator for the free, or NULL for the default.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cyaml_serialize (3),
.BR cyaml_serialize_flow (3),
.BR cyaml_serialize_stream (3)
